 {:name "straight-line-rouche-homotopy-stays-nonzero-on-boundary"
  :lane :solve-lane
  :level :strategy
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Show that the straight-line homotopy from `f` to `f + g` never vanishes on the boundary where `‖g z‖ < ‖f z‖`."
   :statement
   "∀ t : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1, ∀ z ∈ sphere c R, f z + (t.1 : ℂ) * g z ≠ 0"
   :proof-shape
   ["For `t ∈ [0,1]`, establish `‖(t : ℂ)‖ ≤ 1`."
    "If `f z + t * g z = 0`, then norm arithmetic gives `‖f z‖ = ‖t * g z‖ ≤ ‖g z‖`."
    "This contradicts the strict boundary hypothesis `‖g z‖ < ‖f z‖`."]
   :witness
   {:declaration
    "ConstructionTargets.Rouche.rouche_homotopy_ne_zero_on_sphere"
    :axioms ["propext"]
    :sorryAx false}
   :boundary
   "Boundary nonvanishing is the elementary half of the route. It does not by itself prove that the total divisor is constant along the homotopy."
   :capture-kind :runner-narrated-and-commit-witnessed}
  :subjects
  [#:ref{:type :mission, :id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}
   #:ref{:type :construction-target, :id "rouche-root-count-transfer"}
